A||||5||loafer87gt||Need some help with Knackered Headlight....||||1||
Z||000000||loafer87gt||01-02-2000||02:54 AM||||Hi guys, I was just parking my Fiero tonight when I heard a grinding sound and noticed that my passenger side headlight didn't lower and is stuck up. I have heard people talk about the gears going in the headlight assembly and am wondering what parts I will need to fix it, and where I can buy them from. I want to get this fixed PRONTO as I can't stand my car looking like this!! Any info would be appreciated. Also, does anyone know the GM partnumbers for the pieces for an 87GT? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||cobra427||01-02-2000||03:19 AM||||hey loafer, where ya been? Try this as a temp fix while i search out where you can find the parts ok  open the hood and spin the little knob on the top of the motor and see if that doesn't make it go down.  On mine i have to spin it to go up.you just need to give it a little coasing.  Gee, this sounds a little funny doesn't it? Can't wait to see what monkey does with this post. :-)||||reg||1
Z||000002||cobra427||01-02-2000||03:29 AM||||Ok loafer here it is <A HREF="http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/index.html</A>      hope this helps<p>[This message has been edited by cobra427 (edited 01-02-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||cobra427||01-02-2000||03:47 AM||||one more time. Here are the 22P part#'s for the motors:Motor w/actuator RH, 16507926  Motor w/actuator LH,16507925   This is for the 87-88 motors.  Have fun.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||01-02-2000||08:56 AM||||HAHAHA--I'm gonna fool you and give a serious reply this time (1st time for everything! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">).  Instead of buying new headlight motors (expensive), just buy a rebuild kit.  If it's just the gears (sounds like it to me), the rebuild kits are only about $4US/each.  Even if that doesn't do it, you won't be out much money.  I've never done it with headlights (yes, I'm a headlight virgin), but supposedly it only takes about 30min per side.  (Might as well do both sides at the same time.  If one's going out, how long could it be before the other one goes, huh?)||||reg||1
Z||000005||loafer87gt||01-02-2000||01:43 PM||||Thanks a lot for the info guys. I'll give it a try.||||reg||1
